            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nI am not quite sure what is the essence of the issue.\r\n\r\n'mini.jump' defines its own mappings for `f`, `F`, `t`, `T`, `;` making them work across multiple lines. Pressing `dfk` on a line where there is no \"k\" should delete text up until and including the next \"k\" in the lines below.\r\n\r\nWould you mind clarifying what exactly you mean by \"cosumes characters\"? And, please, provide reproducible example which does not alters module's code.",
