            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Sure, here is the minimal config to reproduce the issue:\r\n```lua\r\nvim.cmd [[set runtimepath=$VIMRUNTIME]]\r\nvim.cmd [[set packpath=/tmp/nvt-min/site]]\r\nlocal package_root = \"/tmp/nvt-min/site/pack\"\r\nlocal install_path = package_root .. \"/packer/start/packer.nvim\"\r\nlocal function load_plugins()\r\n  require(\"packer\").startup {\r\n    {\r\n      \"wbthomason/packer.nvim\",\r\n      { 'echasnovski/mini.nvim', branch = 'stable' }\r\n      -- ADD PLUGINS THAT ARE _NECESSARY_ FOR REPRODUCING THE ISSUE\r\n    },\r\n    config = {\r\n      package_root = package_root,\r\n      compile_path = install_path .. \"/plugin/packer_compiled.lua\",\r\n      display = { non_interactive = true },\r\n    },\r\n  }\r\nend\r\nif vim.fn.isdirectory(install_path) == 0 then\r\n  print \"Installing dependencies.\"\r\n  vim.fn.system { \"git\", \"clone\", \"--depth=1\", \"https://github.com/wbthomason/packer.nvim\", install_path }\r\nend\r\nload_plugins()\r\nrequire(\"packer\").sync()\r\nvim.cmd [[autocmd User PackerComplete ++once echo \"Ready!\" | lua setup()]]\r\nvim.opt.termguicolors = true\r\nvim.opt.cursorline = true\r\n\r\n_G.setup = function()\r\n    require('mini.jump').setup()\r\nend\r\n```\r\n\r\nand here is an example input where the issue can be observed:\r\n```\r\nalice bob mark\r\nalice\r\n```\r\n\r\nPut your cursor on the first line, call `dfm`, this will delete all characters up to `m` included. Repeat command using `.` operator. It sometimes works as expected (nothing happens, but you can undo changes and retry the sequence and it will start consuming characters).\r\n\r\n[Kooha-2024-02-11-10-54-08.webm](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/5662622/4d2d0538-ff13-492a-981b-d099b0b68b21)\r\n\r\nYou can also try to delete using a non-existing character like `dfy` (again, it might work when invoked for the first time, just repeat the sequence to see it start consuming characters).\r\n",
