            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks again for finding this issue! It should be fixed on latest `main`.\r\n\r\nThis proved to be not a trivial fix, as it seemed right to make it dot-repeatable even if the target was not found on the first call. This forced to reside with some hackery of undoing the change if it was suspected to be done. Not really a pretty solution, but seems to work in at least most cases.",
